entry.summary:
CogniPrep sells four things, all one-time payments, all digital: access to one assessment provider's games, a feedback upgrade, interview practice, and the assessment centre exercise library. You can see all four priced on the pricing page.
None of them is a Stripe Price at checkout time. Every Checkout Session we create builds its line item inline:
line_items: [{
  price_data: {
    currency: charge.currency,
    product_data: { name, description, ...mp.productData },
    unit_amount: charge.unitAmount,
    ...mp.priceData,
  },
  quantity: 1,
}]

The reason is discounts. A school code, an affiliate link and a provider with a small suite all land on a different unit_amount, and inline price_data lets one code path produce any of them. Pre-made Price objects would mean a Price per amount p…
